 ## Overview
-This method computes the volume of the irregular polyhedron formed by the intersection of a plane and a cube [S1, unofficial]. It is specifically designed for scenarios where a planar boundary slices through a volumetric cell, such as determining the fraction of a cell that is partial ionized or covered by a burning front in computational astrophysics [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard ray-cube intersection by outputting the resulting volume rather than just intersection points, and extends the approach of Salama & Kolb 2005 by explicitly constructing an ordered list of face vertices to facilitate this volume calculation [S1, unofficial].
+This method computes the volume of the irregular polygon formed by the intersection of a plane and a cube [S1, unofficial]. It is specifically designed for scenarios where a planar boundary slices through a volumetric cell, such as determining the fraction of a cell that is partially ionized or covered by a burning front in computational astrophysics [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard ray-cube intersection by outputting the resulting volume rather than just intersection points, and extends the approach of Salama & Kolb 2005 by explicitly constructing an ordered list of face vertices to facilitate this volume calculation [S1, unofficial].
 
